@startuml
' Package diagram — the layers, and the dependencies allowed between them
' Sources: ../../specification/01-architecture.md (section 1), Rule A-1
'
' The layers are in a row, in the order they may depend on each other: a
' layer may only depend on the layers above it.

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #333
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #fbfbfc
  BorderColor #333
  FontColor #333
}

package "Surfaces" as SURF {
  [The workspace\nthe window] as WS
  [The library\norganise] as LIB
  [The definition tab] as DEF
}

package "Process" as PROC {
  [The reader\nserver.py] as SRV
}

package "Services" as SERV {
  [The markdown renderer] as MD
  [The PDF view] as PDF
  [The picture view] as IMG
  [The sheet view] as XLS
  [The word card] as CARD
}

package "Platform\nboundary" as PLAT {
  [The browser's storage\nthe choices, the places] as STORE
  [The browser's document] as DOC
  [The file system's kinds] as KINDS
}

package "Core" as CORE {
  [The kinds of file] as KIND
  [The roots] as ROOTS
  [The rules of a tab] as TABRULES
}

package "Protocol" as PROTO {
  [The reader's routes] as ROUTES
  [The extension's messages] as MESSAGES
}

SURF --> PROC : asks and reads (P-1)
PROC --> SERV : serves the page of a file (A-1)
SERV --> CORE : what a file is, and what a tab is (A-6)
SURF --> CORE : the kinds, the tabs (A-3)
PROC --> PLAT : the disk (D5)
SERV --> PLAT : the browser's document (A-2)
SURF --> PLAT : the browser's storage (A-4)
SURF ..> PROTO : the reader's routes
EXT ..> PROTO : the messages

' the layers, in the order they may depend on each other
SURF -[hidden]-> PROC
PROC -[hidden]-> SERV
SERV -[hidden]-> PLAT
PLAT -[hidden]-> CORE
CORE -[hidden]-> PROTO

note bottom of CORE
  A-4: the state has one owner in each kind.
  The disk belongs to the reader, the choices
  and the places to the browser.
end note

note bottom of PROTO
  A-5: the dependency points one way. The
  extension knows the reader's address; the
  reader does not know the extension exists.
end note
@enduml
